[1m[38;2;0;191;255mDESCRIPTION[0m
[38;5;252mPressing a or r draws the answer box at once, with a blinking cursor as the only motion on screen.[39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPURPOSE[0m
[38;5;252mJørgen 2026-11-18: pressing a changed the footer to 'Enter send' but drew no box; it appeared only[39m
[38;5;252mafter the first keystroke, so nothing showed where to type.                                       [39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPRINCIPLE[0m
[38;5;252mOne consistent 'you are here' indicator: an underline-style cursor that blinks or pulses gently,  [39m
[38;5;252mshared with the pending view-key prefix (v then o/l/b/!). Nothing else on the screen moves or     [39m
[38;5;252mflashes.                                                                                          [39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mRELEVANT DETAILS[0m
[38;5;252mPressing a (answer) or r (request) draws the empty box under the question immediately, with a     [39m
[38;5;252mblinking underline cursor where the text goes; that cursor is the only motion on the otherwise    [39m
[38;5;252mcalm screen.                                                                                      [39m
[38;5;252m                                                                                                  [39m
[38;5;252mCause: answerbox.go openBox() sets m.prompt, resets and focuses the textarea, but never calls     [39m
[38;5;252mm.syncDetail(), so the detail page is not re-rendered with the box; updateAnswer() calls          [39m
[38;5;252msyncDetail() on each key, which is why it appears after typing. Cursor is set static at           [39m
[38;5;252manswerbox.go:30 (cursor.CursorStatic), drawn as a block. Stale 'request qtj177' under the page is [39m
[38;5;252mz82qsy.                                                                                           [39m
